{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves","id":1466540,"title":"Human combat merits for werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-03T17:21:52-07:00","id":1466540,"title":"Human combat merits for werewolves","content":"I was wandering if human combat merits could be applied to an uratha in garou form, I'm thinking about stuff like defensive combat, street fighting and unarmed defense, granted most of these would be redundand or useless when in garou form but stuff like the first level of unarmed defense where you can increase your defense by half the opponent brawl, wouldn't exactly be impossible to apply in garou, what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:25:26-07:00","id":1466542,"title":"","content":"Knee-jerk response is to restrict such \u2018human\u2019 Merits to only Hishu and Dalu forms, but I admit this response is more about aesthetics than mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:32:09-07:00","id":1466547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466542#post1466542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knee-jerk response is to restrict such \u2018human\u2019 Merits to only Hishu and Dalu forms, but I admit this response is more about aesthetics than mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, if you are an expert wrestler or martial artist you are not going to forget everything just because you shifted into garou, some of the dots would be redundant or useless but others would actually make sense. As for the aesthetics, wouldn't an uratha putting a spirit in an armbar before snapping it off be incredibly badass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:44:49-07:00","id":1466551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466547#post1466547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, if you are an expert wrestler or martial artist you are not going to forget everything just because you shifted into garou</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think part of it is a question of whether the shape is necessarily well-suited to the kind of physicality those styles entail, and part of it is that being in Gauru means constantly riding on the edge of literally forgetting yourself and falling into total murder rage as opposed to slightly focused murder rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:45:27-07:00","id":1466553,"title":"","content":"I believe the developers have stated that while you can use Fighting Styles, you are limited to things that require attacks every round, which can limit some of your options.<br /> <br /> Specifically, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445934-fighting-style-in-gauru-ie-kung-fu-panda?p=449064#post449064\">As long as you are meeting the requirements for the Rage restriction, you are free to use Fighting Styles and Merits.</a>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's gauru. And while you may not forget everything, you are full of an inhuman rage that makes you attack anything around you. That said, even with the fighting styles that grant you some extra damage, your claws and fangs will likely be doing more damage than martial arts unless you're using a very good or fetish weapon, and Merits like Living Weapon can guarantee it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-03-2021, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:05:22-07:00","id":1466557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466553#post1466553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the developers have stated that while you can use Fighting Styles, you are limited to things that require attacks every round, which can limit some of your options.<br /> <br /> Specifically, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445934-fighting-style-in-gauru-ie-kung-fu-panda?p=449064#post449064\">As long as you are meeting the requirements for the Rage restriction, you are free to use Fighting Styles and Merits.</a>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> It's gauru. And while you may not forget everything, you are full of an inhuman rage that makes you attack anything around you. That said, even with the fighting styles that grant you some extra damage, your claws and fangs will likely be doing more damage than martial arts unless you're using a very good or fetish weapon, and Merits like Living Weapon can guarantee it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't see any developers in the post you linked (I apologize if <i>I'm wrong) also, dodging and defense would count as attacking (I didn't read anywhere in the book that you can't defend in garou form), the way I interpret it is that in garou form you have to actively engage or otherwise work toward harming your target (you can sneak up on a target for a stealth attack in garou form from what I know) but nothing says you can't be tactical and smart about it, urathas in garou are not mindless beasts, while they are on the tether of rage, they can still recognize friend from foe and would still be smart enough to be more efficient in dispatching their pray.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:12:17-07:00","id":1466558,"title":"","content":"Heh, armbar-ing a spirit before biting its head off is cool, I admit. Though it\u2019s also likely that someone could say that \u201cIsn\u2019t that just a flourished Brawl roll?\u201d If you\u2019re the ST, you\u2019ve gotta decide some things. <br /> <br /> In the above link by nofather; Acrozatarim is the mentioned writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:14:40-07:00","id":1466559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466557#post1466557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see any developers in the post you linked (I apologize if <i>I'm wrong)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The quote and link was to Acrozatarim, one of our werewolf developers and writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:20:25-07:00","id":1466560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466559#post1466559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The quote and link was to Acrozatarim, one of our werewolf developers and writers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize then, still, my point toward the &quot;attack&quot; part still stand, unless a developer could come and clarify or you can point me to a thread where its specified what the rage restriction actually entails (not being aggressive btw, <i>I honestly want to know about this).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:20:33-07:00","id":1466561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466557#post1466557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the way I interpret it is that in garou form you have to actively engage or otherwise work toward harming your target (you can sneak up on a target for a stealth attack in garou form from what I know) but nothing says you can't be tactical and smart about it, urathas in garou are not mindless beasts, while they are on the tether of rage, they can still recognize friend from foe and would still be smart enough to be more efficient in dispatching their pray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can shapeshift and Gauru is the Killing Form. If you need to sneak up on something, you sneak up on it in a form that isn't a <i>nine-foot-tall killing machine </i>that &quot;must strike an active opponent within striking range each turn&quot; or else roll to avoid falling immediately into the uncontrolled rage-state where, no, they <i>can't</i> tell friend from foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:23:51-07:00","id":1466563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466558#post1466558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, armbar-ing a spirit before biting its head off is cool, I admit. Though it\u2019s also likely that someone could say that \u201cIsn\u2019t that just a flourished Brawl roll?\u201d If you\u2019re the ST, you\u2019ve gotta decide some things.<br /> <br /> In the above link by nofather; Acrozatarim is the mentioned writer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Flourished rolls are a call of the story teller (I had an ST in a human game that treated most one shot kills by gunfire as an headshot, no rules he just liked the aesthetic of it), actually putting a spirit in an armbar so that one of your packmates could finish it off would be an actual move (and a badass one at that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:27:04-07:00","id":1466564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466561#post1466561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can shapeshift and Gauru is the Killing Form. If you need to sneak up on something, you sneak up on it in a form that isn't a <i>nine-foot-tall killing machine </i>that &quot;must strike an active opponent within striking range each turn&quot; or else roll to avoid falling immediately into the uncontrolled rage-state where, no, they <i>can't</i> tell friend from foe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If this were the case then everytime a spirit or something else manage to dodge an attack (rare but not impossible) then the garou should roll for not falling to rage, I don't know if this was the developers intentions but It would need some better clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:31:51-07:00","id":1466565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466563#post1466563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Flourished rolls are a call of the story teller (I had an ST in a human game that treated most one shot kills by gunfire as an headshot, no rules he just liked the aesthetic of it), actually putting a spirit in an armbar so that one of your packmates could finish it off would be an actual move (and a badass one at that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in the line of;<br /> \u201cHey, I wanna do this cool choke move in Gauru too; I already bought a Merit for that\u201d<br /> \u201cSure, but you didn\u2019t need too \u2014 I mean, you could just roll Strength + Brawl normally\u201d<br /> \u201cBut I thought this Merit was necessary?\u201d<br /> \u201cBah, puny humans\u201d<br /> <br /> Buuut anyways, the writers already clarified we can use Merits if they fit, so we\u2019re all free to go all out on them.<br /> Of course, the Rage thing makes a good number of them rather unfit\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:31:56-07:00","id":1466566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466560#post1466560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize then, still, my point toward the &quot;attack&quot; part still stand, unless a developer could come and clarify or you can point me to a thread where its specified what the rage restriction actually entails (not being aggressive btw, <i>I honestly want to know about this).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's no biggie, I just think your response was suggesting I said something I didn't say. I didn't say anything about dodging or defense, or werewolves not being tactical or smart in Gauru form, I didn't say they were mindless beasts. To be more clear, some fighting style merits require you to not attack for a turn. This wouldn't be an option if you were lingering in gauru.<br /> <br /> Regarding what Gauru says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;A Gauru-form Uratha must attack an active opponent within striking range each turn. She does not have to continue to attack a crippled opponent as long as another opponent exists. If an opponent is out of reach, she can move toward or throw things at opponent. If she has no opponents, she will attack anything she can reach. If she does anything else, roll Resolve + Composure or fall into Kuruth.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And while in regular Gauru form they can choose between friend or foe, once they hit Kuruth they generally cannot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:40:54-07:00","id":1466570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466566#post1466566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's no biggie, I just think your response was suggesting I said something I didn't say. I didn't say anything about dodging or defense, or werewolves not being tactical or smart in Gauru form, I didn't say they were mindless beasts. To be more clear, some fighting style merits require you to not attack for a turn. This wouldn't be an option if you were lingering in gauru.<br /> <br /> Regarding what Gauru says:<br /> <br /> <br /> And while in regular Gauru form they can choose between friend or foe, once they hit Kuruth they generally cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What constitute an &quot;attack&quot; is my question, if you are fighting a particularly powerful spirit and it has already dealt enough lethal damage to turn it into aggravated, what would an uratha do? keep attacking like a moron or fight more defensively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:43:19-07:00","id":1466572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466565#post1466565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant in the line of;<br /> \u201cHey, I wanna do this cool choke move in Gauru too; I already bought a Merit for that\u201d<br /> \u201cSure, but you didn\u2019t need too \u2014 I mean, you could just roll Strength + Brawl normally\u201d<br /> \u201cBut I thought this Merit was necessary?\u201d<br /> \u201cBah, puny humans\u201d<br /> <br /> Buuut anyways, the writers already clarified we can use Merits if they fit, so we\u2019re all free to go all out on them.<br /> Of course, the Rage thing makes a good number of them rather unfit\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If its a flourish thing to finish an opponent sure but if its aim to immobilize it, actually choke it or apply other merits, there are merits for that, not for humans of course but for some of the more powerfull spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:57:11-07:00","id":1466574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466572#post1466572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If its a flourish thing to finish an opponent sure but if its aim to immobilize it, actually choke it or apply other merits, there are merits for that, not for humans of course but for some of the more powerfull spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And\u2026 yes? Before I was \u201cWe can just use the normal grappling rules for that; not being able to use grappling-Merits in Gauru isn\u2019t that much of a loss.\u201d After seeing the above link to Acrozatarim, now I\u2019m like \u201cYay break out Hurt Locker.\u201d We can just roll with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:05:03-07:00","id":1466577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466570#post1466570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What constitute an &quot;attack&quot; is my question, if you are fighting a particularly powerful spirit and it has already dealt enough lethal damage to turn it into aggravated, what would an uratha do? keep attacking like a moron or fight more defensively?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how attacking wounded prey would make the attacker 'like a moron.' Letting it sit with Health at Aggravated can just give it time to run away and wait for your Gauru to wear off, or use all its Essence to overload a Blast attack. And in this case you've already taken Gauru form, which is &quot;is a form to take and to dodge killing blows, and to end a hunt or a battle quickly and efficiently.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, attacks are pretty clearly listed in the Attack section of the Combat sections of the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On each character\u2019s turn, he can attack using one of the following dice pools:<br /> \u2022 Unarmed Combat: Strength + Brawl - opponent\u2019s Defense<br /> \u2022 Melee Combat: Strength + Weaponry - opponent\u2019s Defense<br /> \u2022 Ranged Combat: Dexterity + Firearms<br /> \u2022 Thrown Weapons: Dexterity + Athletics - opponent\u2019s Defense </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:23:15-07:00","id":1466581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466564#post1466564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this were the case then everytime a spirit or something else manage to dodge an attack (rare but not impossible) then the garou should roll for not falling to rage,</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a wide wide gulf of difference between &quot;strike means successfully hit&quot; and &quot;strike means make an attack roll&quot; and it is nevertheless not a gap in which there is legitimate interpretive room for &quot;do something that isn't trying to hit an enemy or moving into range to do so&quot; to fit the bill for a state called Rage that is an intrinsic part of Gauru form as it is encountered by default. If you want to do other stuff in Gauru, The Father's Form costs one Experience to develop and has a whopping prerequisite of Purity 1, but again, there are other forms better-suited to most other stuff and they aren't metered as starkly as the Killing Form is.<br /> <br /> (The name of the form is Gauru. Garou is a different Werewolf game altogether.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T03:24:48-07:00","id":1466626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466577#post1466577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how attacking wounded prey would make the attacker 'like a moron.' Letting it sit with Health at Aggravated can just give it time to run away and wait for your Gauru to wear off, or use all its Essence to overload a Blast attack. And in this case you've already taken Gauru form, which is &quot;is a form to take and to dodge killing blows, and to end a hunt or a battle quickly and efficiently.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, attacks are pretty clearly listed in the Attack section of the Combat sections of the books.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant the uratha being wounded not the prey, sure its rare but every once in a while a powerfull spirit will get the upperhand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T05:04:51-07:00","id":1466636,"title":"","content":"This topic did come up in our game.<br /> <br /> We ended up ruling that since Brawl is used for attacks in all five forms, then Defensive Combat works in any of the five forms as well.<br /> <br /> For other fighting styles we ruled that anything that reasonably sounds like it relies on human physiology is restricted to Hishu and Dalu forms, as is any style that uses a weapon (for obvious reasons). To give some examples, Close Quarters Combat and Choke Hold (with teeth) are probably fine in any of the forms. Some styles like Grappling have manoeuvres that would probably still work in wolf form (the first two dots) and ones that probably wouldn't (Joint Lock). We ruled that styles like Martial Arts and Boxing require a human physiology.<br /> <br /> We never explicitly ruled on whether you can use human combat styles in Gauru form, but I think the understanding was that things like Boxing still wouldn't work, in part due to how inhuman the form is, and in part because the level of control needed to execute these manoeuvres is not present in Gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T09:26:55-07:00","id":1466661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466540-human-combat-merits-for-werewolves?p=1466636#post1466636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This topic did come up in our game.<br /> <br /> We ended up ruling that since Brawl is used for attacks in all five forms, then Defensive Combat works in any of the five forms as well.<br /> <br /> For other fighting styles we ruled that anything that reasonably sounds like it relies on human physiology is restricted to Hishu and Dalu forms, as is any style that uses a weapon (for obvious reasons). To give some examples, Close Quarters Combat and Choke Hold (with teeth) are probably fine in any of the forms. Some styles like Grappling have manoeuvres that would probably still work in wolf form (the first two dots) and ones that probably wouldn't (Joint Lock). We ruled that styles like Martial Arts and Boxing require a human physiology.<br /> <br /> We never explicitly ruled on whether you can use human combat styles in Gauru form, but I think the understanding was that things like Boxing still wouldn't work, in part due to how inhuman the form is, and in part because the level of control needed to execute these manoeuvres is not present in Gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my reasoning too, not all the dots of merits would work in garou form but things like the first dot of the unarmed defense merit, would apply because they are supposed to be instinctive and not tied to human physiology. I started this thread because I realized that my character is pretty weak in hishu form and since the game is set in a big city with lots of cameras and witnesses, she can't exactly shift to garou or even dalu everytime some asshole try to pick a fight, so I wanted to buy some merits to deal with this and wondered if it would be something restricted only to hishu and dalu or if they could be used (to some extent at least) even in garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}